  "verdict": "No new supported API defect in the manually inspected contracts; source disposition only.",
  "findings": [],
  "contracts": [
    {
      "topic": "Package and public paths",
      "disposition": "consistent",
      "detail": "phantom-http declares lib phantom; the client inventory namespace is correct. A58 canonical root/request exports and retired aliases are intentional; private definition paths printed by the generator do not establish import defects."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Feature and dependency boundary",
      "disposition": "consistent in inspected scope",
      "detail": "Manifests/export roots gate optional DNS, cookies, JSON, SSE, WebSocket, diagnostics and danger exposure. Documented bytes/http/http-body, Tokio, profile/provider and optional stream/serde public dependencies match signatures. These all-feature inventories do not establish default-feature or Send/Sync compilation."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Base URL and header hooks",
      "disposition": "supported by declaring and caller source",
      "detail": "BaseUrl validates scheme/authority before storing configuration, joins relative references and preserves absolute targets. RequestBuilder resolves before building the request. Client hooks precede request hooks and template checks in send_inner; recoverable hook errors retain the original source. Hook mutation validates before changing ordered fields; hook docs explicitly limit redirect credential protection."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Admission",
      "disposition": "unbounded NonZeroUsize panic candidate rejected",
      "detail": "Client build calls policy validation, which rejects active/pending semaphore bounds above MAX_PERMITS. Actual protocol pool admission functions use the concrete registry; permits own admission and release by Drop. This is a bounded source assessment, not runtime fairness/cancellation proof."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Routes",
      "disposition": "consistent in inspected scope",
      "detail": "Route docs distinguish TCP CONNECT from QUIC/CONNECT-UDP. The request compatibility match rejects unsupported scheme/protocol/route combinations; explicit HTTP2 fallback also checks the route. No general production fallback or all-route proof is inferred from these ranges."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Bodies and concrete causes",
      "disposition": "consistent in inspected scope",
      "detail": "RequestBody captures metadata without polling, preserves source errors, checks emitted length and exact terminal trailer names/count/bytes. ResponseBody collection uses a byte bound and closes the wire body on excess; driver cleanup remains qualified. RequestError and Http1TlsError preserve concrete nested causes, so direct first-source downcast is not universally valid."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Hidden address-family and slower-connection types",
      "disposition": "inaccessible return-type candidate rejected",
      "detail": "tcp publicly reexports AddressFamilyMemory/SlowerConnection; their declaring owner explicitly marks them doc(hidden) facade pool seams. Their omission from the generated inventory is not absence of a public path or a promised supported consumer API."
    }
  ],
